Third-party components
----------------------
Kerotakis links or embeds the following. All are permissively licensed and
compatible with AGPL-3.0 distribution; their notices are preserved per their
respective terms.

Engines
- IPhreeqc / PHREEQC — public domain (U.S. Geological Survey). Aqueous
  speciation, mineral saturation, gas partitioning and redox. Embedded together
  with its thermodynamic databases (phreeqc.dat, wateq4f.dat, minteq.v4.dat),
  which are likewise public domain.
- Indigo — Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) EPAM Systems. Structure handling, canonical
  identity and reaction product enumeration.
- CoolProp — MIT, Copyright (c) Ian Bell et al. Pure-component thermophysical
  properties, via the coolprop-sys bindings.
- diffsol — MIT, Copyright (c) Martin Robinson. Stiff ODE/DAE integration for
  reaction kinetics.

Reactivity data
- CAMEO Chemicals reactive-group compatibility matrix — U.S. Government work,
  produced by NOAA's Office of Response and Restoration with the EPA and the
  Center for Chemical Process Safety.

Rust crates
- The full dependency set and its licenses are reproduced in-app under
  About -> Open-source licenses, generated from cargo-about.

Build-time only (not distributed with binaries)
- xtb / CREST — LGPL-3.0, Copyright (c) Grimme group. Used offline to compute
  reaction energetics that are baked into the curated library as data. Neither
  binary nor library is shipped, so no LGPL-3.0 relinking obligation attaches to
  distributed builds.
